From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:23:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq807x: add support for Zyxel WAX650S

The Zyxel WAX650S is an 802.11ax access point with a 5 GbE uplink. It is
built like the NWA210AX (flash layout, LEDs, reset button, 1 GbE port
and dual-image boot), with an IPQ8072A and an AQR114C uplink PHY.

Hardware
--------
SoC:      Qualcomm IPQ8072A
RAM:      1 GiB DDR3
Flash:    8 MiB SPI-NOR, 256 MiB SPI-NAND
WLAN:     2.4 GHz QCN5024 4x4, 5 GHz QCN5054 4x4
          QCA9889 1x1 on PCIe (uncalibrated, used by the stock firmware
          for zero-wait DFS only; left disabled)
Ethernet: Uplink: 5 GbE AQR114C (USXGMII), 802.3at/bt PoE input
          LAN1: 1 GbE QCA8033
LEDs:     4-colour LP5562, 2 GPIO LEDs
Buttons:  Reset
Power:    12 V DC or PoE

The smart antenna, the CC2640R2F Bluetooth module and the stock PoE
power modes are not supported. The stock firmware drops both radios to
2 TX chains when powered by 802.3at; OpenWrt runs them at 4x4, so use
802.3bt or the DC jack.

Uplink PHY firmware
-------------------
The AQR114C has no flash of its own. The stock bootloader loads its
firmware on every boot from the "ethphyfw" UBI volume of the "rootfs"
partition, the one OpenWrt is installed to. The OpenWrt image carries
an "ethphyfw" volume with a placeholder; on first boot a preinit script
copies the firmware from the stock image in "rootfs_1", which the
installation keeps, and reboots once. Sysupgrade keeps the volume.
Until then, and if the stock image is gone, only LAN1 works. The PHY
has no reset GPIO in the device tree, as a reset would clear the
firmware.

The volume comes first in the UBI image, so the root filesystem is
ubiblock0_2.

Installation, Switch Boot Image and MAC addresses are as on the
NWA210AX; the factory image carries model ID 54 e1.

The firmware itself is not redistributable, so the image cannot ship
it.

Tested on a WAX650S: the first boot copies the PHY firmware and
reboots, the bootloader then starts the PHY and the uplink links at
1 GbE (the only speed the switch port offered), and both radios
beacon with the new board data. Not yet tested: 2.5/5 GbE, LAN1 and
Wi-Fi clients.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
